{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=8{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=8{b}_{1}-5{b}_{2}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15ec9ef4f3eac7062fdfee991e546dfc959561c7a2bcba47399f1f5b73521296"} {"question" "q-38086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15ec9ef4f3eac7062fdfee991e546dfc959561c7a2bcba47399f1f5b73521296"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 3 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15ec9ef4f3eac7062fdfee991e546dfc959561c7a2bcba47399f1f5b73521296"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{6} & 2 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-38918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{6} & \\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ $T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15ec9ef4f3eac7062fdfee991e546dfc959561c7a2bcba47399f1f5b73521296"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & c \\\\ a & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & b & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x-y+z \\\\ x+y \\\\ y-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2},$ and ${b}_{3}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{2} & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ $c=2$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+2=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15ec9ef4f3eac7062fdfee991e546dfc959561c7a2bcba47399f1f5b73521296"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"} {"question" "q-82496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070151/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec16089f4620807d807c8fe47731ea58c76d7c50f8bbc7ba695cfaeb5337c93f"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2454 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
